  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">48hrs 3rd Envelope Emergency Response Plan for Syria: Rapid Health Services, Hygiene, and Essential Aid Deployment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtIn Latakia, SARC will focus on WASH and Health interventions. Rapid rehabilitation works will restore access to safe water through the provision of electric cables for the fifth pumping station replacement of electric transformers, and provision of polyethylene pipelines. Soft WASH activities will complement this by distributing 20L jerrycans and MHM kits to affected households. Health assistance will be provided through the Establishment of Primary Health Care (PHC) services, addressing both immediate and longer-term needs in hard-to-reach areas such as Al-Basit. The PHC unit will cover a wide network of villages, ensuring delivery of essential medical services to the most vulnerable.ltbrgtIn both the wildfires-affected areas, SARC will address urgent Food Security and SNFI needs. Assistance will include the distribution of food parcels, and Cash for shelter ensuring the dignity and well-being of affected communities while meeting their immediate basic needs.ltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtltbrgtBased on the Health situation in As- Sweida, SARC will refunction, Najran PHC that covers about 24 surrounding villages in 7 k.m diameter.ltbrgtHealth assistance will be provided through the Establishment of Primary Health Care (PHC) services, addressing both immediate and longer-term needs in hard-to-reach areas. The PHC unit will cover a wide network of villages, ensuring delivery of essential medical services to the most vulnerable. In addition, the PHC will be the nearest health emergency point in the area.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
